From 15b755ada267e41d897912fcf617dbceb027a24c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sayzal28 <Sayzal28@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:46:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Race outfits: the African picture has to line up with the
 European one below the neck

The 14 Oct line-up check (outfit_lineup/build.py) now runs in the api on every
African try, after the size, cut-out and head checks. It fails when clothes or
skin moved more than 10 px. The same model then draws it again. When no try is
left, the try that moved least becomes the picture and the log says the check
failed (clothes.lineup kept closest). The European step and Studio costumes are
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
